  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Marsabit Resilience Livelihoods Project -CM-RLP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Marsabit Resilience livelihood project is a 3 year project with an annual funding of &#xa3;50,000 from CAFOD General Funds effective 1st April 2023 to 31st March 2026, currently in its third year of implementation. The project will contribute to the CAFOD  Kenya Uganda new programme strategy with the overall goal of building Resilient communities in which people, particularly women and girls, thrive in a peaceful, well-governed, and healthy, supportive natural environment.
The project overall goal is to contribute to improved food security, good governance and building resilience for the drought affected population in Marsabit County. This will be achieved through 3 closely interrelated outcome areas, namely;
 1. Improved and diversified livelihood options for resilient target communities.
2.  Increased community capacity to effectively manage and protect natural resources
3. Increased community participation on good governance 

This project puts protection, safeguarding and accountability at the heart of our work. From the analysis of the context, capacities and vulnerabilities of the diverse groups, this project targets  4 groups with bee keeping, 5 groups with poultry production, 5 groups with saving and lending, 2 groups provided with shade nets, 2 groups with hydroponic farming technique, 5 groups  trained on rangeland management, 4 groups trained on nursery management, support dissemination of early warning systems through radio talk shows and support lobby and  advocacy skills, public participation, budget making process and accountability forums in 2 wards. . The resilience project will be implemented in two wards of Saku and Moyale sub counties of the larger Marsabit County.</narrative>
  </description>
